From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 03:26:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: base: attach the Mac UI pump to a host run loop

Open Arc runs Chromium's browser process inside an app whose
NSApplication (SwiftUI's) already runs the main run loop. Upstream Mac
code can only start the UI thread by Run()-ing its MessagePump, which
would call -[NSApplication run] itself or nest a loop that never
returns to the app.

iOS has the model we need: the UI pump is attached to the platform's
loop with CurrentUIThread::Attach() and pushes an outer RunLoop without
running it. This extends that path to MessagePumpNSApplication:

- MessagePumpNSApplication::Attach()/Detach(): set the delegate, mark
  an outer RunLoop as running, and account for a CFRunLoop run already
  on the stack so the enter/exit observer stays balanced. A Quit() of
  the attached outer level is ignored: the app quits via NSApplication.
  Nested RunLoops still go through DoRun() as before.
- CurrentUIThread::Attach() and a new Mac-only Detach(), plus the
  SequenceManager / ThreadController plumbing (IS_IOS -> also IS_MAC).
- The controller detaches only a pump it attached, so normal Mac
  embedders (Chrome, content_shell) are unaffected.

Needed by plan task C6 (//openarc embedder start). Without it the
embedder would have to own the app's main loop.
